            <div xml:id="d445">

                <pb facs="0679" n="577" sameAs="frus:frus1935v01/pg577"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">883.05/554: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Egypt</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Fish</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1936-01-13T15:00:00-05:00">January 13, 1936—3
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2. Your 1, January 7, 11 a.m. You may advise the Foreign Office that this
                    Government accepts the proposed amendment to the Regulations for the Judicial
                    Organization, the text of which was set forth in the note of the Minister for
                    Foreign Affairs of July 10, 1935.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
